-- title:
--   Node ring elements are A∩ K constants modulo non-units
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{red}:A\to k$ a ring homomorphism; let `data` be a modular polynomial datum for $q$ (a monic $\Phi\in\mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ vanishing on the pair of $q$-expansions of $j$) satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \bmod q=(X^q-Y)(X-Y^q)$, let $h\alpha,h\beta$ assert integrality of the two degeneracy embeddings from level $1$ to level $q$, and let $P$ be a place specialisation of this data at level $N=1$ with reduction $\mathrm{red}$. Let $R$ be a prolongation tuple over $P$, let $q\ge 5$, assume the order law `R.OrderLawFixed`, let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,1$ all of which are supersingular (rational, affine for the two geometric $j$-generators, with $j$-value in the supersingular set), and assume the regularity law `R.RegularityLaw W`. Let $K\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$, let $w\in W$, let $V$ be a place of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-modular function field of level $1\cdot q$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V=w$, and suppose the value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,k\,1)$ lies in the image of $A\cap K$ under $\mathrm{red}$. Then for every $g$ in the ring $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K\,w$ — the elements of the level-$q$ function field that are integral for $R.R_1$, for $R.R_2$ and at every place reducing to $w$, and whose Laurent expansion lies in the subfield generated by the constants of $K$ together with the two $j$-expansions — there is $o\in A\cap K$ such that $g-R.\mathrm{nodeConst}\,K\,w\,o$ is not a unit of that ring, where $R.\mathrm{nodeConst}$ sends $o$ to its image under the structure map of the function field.
--
--   This is the residue-surjectivity statement for the ring of $K$-rational node integers at a supersingular point of $X_0(q)$ in characteristic $q$: the residue map of that local ring is already hit by the constants of $A\cap K$, which reflects the Deligne–Rapoport description of the integral model of $X_0(q)$ at the supersingular points. It is used in the level-one construction of inertia-fixed node coordinates and in the ensuing computation with the component group and the depth pairing.
